  "slug": "kinetic-decomposition-pathways-reciprocal-2328",
  "summary": "Recent benchmarks and force-field corrections target rare RNA conformations and variant-level structural ambiguity in computational models.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational access to conformational states that are rare, intermediate, or poorly constrained by a single static model. One preprint benchmarks enhanced-sampling MD (T-REMD, REST2, GaMD) and structure-prediction methods for RNA ensembles on HIV-1 TAR, validated by RDC and QM/MM comparisons. A second develops gHBfix-18Ab, an 18-component hydrogen-bond correction for AMBER RNA force fields that restores the NMR-observed stacked state of the MAPT A-bulge motif. A third compares AlphaFold2 models of POLG R627Q and W748S, placing the changes within model-variability range. What is new is the emphasis on controlling method error, through NMR-guided reparameterization and explicit variability controls. The set is heterogeneous: the first two address dynamic ensembles directly, while the POLG analysis concerns static prediction uncertainty.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-08-30"
}
